Subject: [PATCH 1/2] bench.placement: a shared public IP (a datacenter's
 egress NAT) is separate machines only with machine id, DMI product_uuid and
 boot_id all recorded and all different, a measured RTT >= RTT_FLOOR_MS (0.1
 ms; co-residence measured 0.03) and no host bridge (loopback, link-local,
 docker 172.16/12 always refused; a routed 10.x network is fine between
 distinct machine ids); plan requires differing machine ids and records the
 rest as pending; register records cell.placement.shared_public_ip with the
 three ids and the RTT (coordinator 22:00Z); tests: the NAT pair accepted, the
 co-resident pair and every missing proof refused

Co-authored-by: danielreuter <danielreuter@users.noreply.github.com>
